## Context

[The review of #4471](/kb/incidents/4471-review) finds distinct parser and booking-form hint
failures in a ticket described as one issue. Subject matching hides that distinction. The old
[accepted decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) is preserved unchanged.

## Proposed replacement

Use the failure mechanism as the duplicate key. Read the body and resolve tenant locale, form
version and input channel. Subject and intake tags help search; neither proves a duplicate.
Where the supplied classifier cannot place a report, retain it separately and gather missing context.

<DedupeExplorer />

## Consequences and acceptance

Triage requires more context but avoids merging distinct bugs and splitting the same bug by wording.
Keep explicit report IDs and per-cause counts so export overlap cannot inflate impact.
Preserve contradictory observations as follow-ups instead of forcing a new technical diagnosis.
This record remains proposed until the support owner accepts it; it does not claim that the desk's
live policy or queue has already changed.

